WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.371 --> 00:00:07.018
- I'm Famo Musa, I'm a refugee,
and also I'm a mother of two.

00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:10.997
I'm a student and I would
say I'm a photographer.

00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:14.080
I don't know, I'm just a human being.

00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:25.700
I was born in Somalia
but I grew up in Kenya.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.783
I came here back in 2004
when I was 12 years old.

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:37.521
- Let’s see if there's any
other like, action ones.

00:00:37.521 --> 00:00:40.246
- I met the AjA Project
when I was in middle school.

00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:41.622
I was in 8th grade.

00:00:41.622 --> 00:00:45.515
It's a group of youth and
some adults who are working

00:00:45.515 --> 00:00:47.978
on improving the community.

00:00:47.978 --> 00:00:50.390
They teach you how to take
pictures and how to tell

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.761
your story, and at the same
time giving voices to people

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:56.815
who don't have the opportunity
to tell their stories.

00:00:56.815 --> 00:00:59.436
I got fascinated 'cause
I didn't speak English,

00:00:59.436 --> 00:01:02.686
so I used photography to tell my story.

00:01:04.424 --> 00:01:08.053
The way I capture images
changed throughout time.

00:01:08.053 --> 00:01:10.786
I guess at first when I
didn't have the digital camera

00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:13.405
it was like, you have to
go develop your images

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:14.864
and then come back, and then you're like

00:01:14.864 --> 00:01:16.713
ooh I don't like that buy another roll

00:01:16.713 --> 00:01:17.719
and then take it again.

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:20.695
Now you have the DSLR,
where you just take a picture

00:01:20.695 --> 00:01:23.622
and then it automatically
goes to your computer.

00:01:23.622 --> 00:01:26.800
Before that they had
this big computers to put

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.276
the memory card in the computer.

00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:31.794
You have to use a wire and then
plug it, it was complicated.

00:01:31.794 --> 00:01:33.955
Now it's much simpler.

00:01:33.955 --> 00:01:36.847
Photography and technology,
they go hand in hand.

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:40.007
Not having technology is very different.

00:01:40.007 --> 00:01:43.016
Back home we didn't have any cameras.

00:01:43.016 --> 00:01:45.142
We couldn't just go to the
store and buy a camera,

00:01:45.142 --> 00:01:47.326
even the disposable ones.

00:01:47.326 --> 00:01:50.009
So we didn't have pictures of us younger.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:53.470
Like my mom, she doesn't know
what she look like back then.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.747
I don't know what I look
like when I was a baby.

00:01:55.747 --> 00:01:58.784
We don't have any photos,
so I wanted to change that

00:01:58.784 --> 00:01:59.784
for my kids.

00:02:01.071 --> 00:02:02.870
The Famo who is mother

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.674
and then the Famo who's a photographer.

00:02:04.674 --> 00:02:08.006
The one thing they have in
common it’s saving memories.

00:02:08.006 --> 00:02:10.226
Things become history in like a second,

00:02:10.226 --> 00:02:14.189
so that's why I love taking
pictures all the time.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:17.041
When people think of refugee
they don't go out there

00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:19.310
to ask a refugee person.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.523
Every group has like, the little box

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:23.125
that people put them in.

00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.906
Each person has to be able
to tell you who they are

00:02:25.906 --> 00:02:27.529
and where they come from.

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:31.271
A computer gives you a way
to connect with the world.

00:02:31.271 --> 00:02:35.461
I want the next generation
to be open minded,

00:02:35.461 --> 00:02:39.039
to follow their dreams, not
to let anybody speak for them.

00:02:39.039 --> 00:02:41.539
(light music)

